# Testing & Deploy Culture (NO EXCEPTIONS)

## Tests are part of the change

- Bugfixes and non-trivial behavior changes **ship with a regression test** in the same turn
- Cover edge cases: null/empty, auth 401/403, admin vs organizer paths, unpaid/paused payouts, mobile layout regressions
- Do **not** end a deep-review turn with “follow up with tests later”

## Layout (Vitest — two projects)

| Layer | Glob | Env |
|-------|------|-----|
| API unit / integration | `api/**/*.test.ts`, `api/**/*.integration.test.ts` | node |
| Unit helpers | `tests/unit/**/*.spec.ts`, `app/**/*.spec.ts` | node |
| Remaining smoke | `tests/smoke/**/*.spec.ts` | node |
| UI components | `**/*.spec.tsx`, `tests/integration/**` | jsdom |

- Mock HTTP suites: `setTestPool()` via `tests/helpers/*Harness.ts`
- Real TiDB integration: `api/testDbCleanup.ts`, unique `@test.local` emails, cleanup in `afterAll`
- `VITEST=true` + `ATLEITA_TEST_MODE=1` in `vitest.config.ts`

## Deploy gate

- Production: `npm run deploy:prod` (not raw `vercel --prod` alone)
- Pre-deploy: `check:api-inline` → `typecheck` → `test` → Vercel → `app_version`
- Skip checks only when user explicitly passes `--skip-checks`

## Commands

- `npm test` — full suite
- `npm run test:api` — API tests only
- `npm run check:api-inline` — Vercel bundle gate
- `npm run test:cleanup-fixtures` — purge leftover `@test.local` rows from TiDB
